From: gsm-system folk/uhd4
Subject: [PATCH] SIP: adapt ortp log hook to bctbx (ortp>=4) signature
Date: Sat, 6 Sep 2026

ortp>=4 routes ortp_set_log_handler through bctbx, whose handler
takes a domain first arg:
  old: void (*)(OrtpLogLevel, const char *, va_list)
  new: void (*)(const char *domain, BctbxLogLevel, const char *, va_list)
Adapt the one hook (domain ignored, as before with lev).

--- a/SIP/SIP2Interface.cpp
+++ b/SIP/SIP2Interface.cpp
@@ -715,7 +715,8 @@
 // Pat added to hook messages from the ORTP library.  See ortp_set_log_handler in ortp.c.
+// (folk/uhd4: ortp>=4 routes logging through bctbx; handler gains domain.)
 extern "C" {
-	static void ortpLogFunc(OrtpLogLevel /*lev unused*/, const char *fmt, va_list args)
+	static void ortpLogFunc(const char * /*domain unused*/, BctbxLogLevel /*lev unused*/, const char *fmt, va_list args)
 	{
 		// This floods the system with error messages, so regulate output to the console.
 		static time_t lasttime = 0;	// No more than one message per minute.
